      },
      "message": "refactor(norm-rules): Standardize naming for implementation-defined behaviors\n\nConvert normative rule parameter definitions to use impl-def-behavior\nproperty and uppercase naming convention to align with Parameter SIG\nrequirements.\n\nChanges:\n- Uppercase 205 normative rule names with impl-def-behavior: true across\n  11 YAML files (counters, f-st-ext, hypervisor, machine, priv-csrs,\n  smctr, supervisor, v-st-ext, zc, zihintntl, zilsd)\n- Convert hyphens to underscores in all uppercased names\n- Replace \"kind: parameter\" with \"impl-def-behavior: true\" (61 entries\n  in machine.yaml)\n- Update 11 normative tag names to use underscores instead of hyphens\n  in both YAML definitions and AsciiDoc source files for consistency\n- Remove \"instances\" field from pmp_granularity_param rule\n- Update terminology from \"parameters\" to \"implementation-defined\n  behaviors\" in tagging_normative_rules.adoc\n\nFiles affected:\n- 11 YAML normative rule definition files\n- 5 AsciiDoc source files (hypervisor, machine, supervisor, v-st-ext,\n  zihintntl)\n- Updated reference JSON files for norm tags\n- Added documentation files: normative_rule_name_changes.md,\n  tag_name_changes.md\n\nAll changes validated with `make build-norm-rules` - builds successfully\nwith pattern ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+$ enforced for impl-def-behavior names.\n\nExamples:\n- misa_csr_implemented → MISA_CSR_IMPLEMENTED\n- satp-asidlen → SATP_ASIDLEN\n- critical-error → CRITICAL_ERROR\n- kind: parameter → impl-def-behavior: true\n- norm:hgatp-vmid_param → norm:hgatp_vmid_param\n\nRelated to issue #2669\n\nSigned-off-by: James Ball <jameball@qti.qualcomm.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "d2cc11fb6e1b3d414fd6f565d6979557043b893f",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/git/trees/d2cc11fb6e1b3d414fd6f565d6979557043b893f"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/git/commits/2cc540bd2cbabc7128052b7914311237dcc81235",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg16IhvCOzptStJPlQoeFl2EpLYG\najietOw2H6wA83wCwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDlg8cyJHmSxCSB6+1IEIcmnIlCLGUe0hPyV81qjHUA6c4AIfJdCVeLsd5/Pe6/z4N\nskzkWQM+ZArf67zs2iWA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree d2cc11fb6e1b3d414fd6f565d6979557043b893f\nparent 9a877ab98936049e15ae84c1e92f087e497ef882\nauthor James Ball <jameball@qti.qualcomm.com> 1771196871 -0800\ncommitter James Ball <jameball@qti.qualcomm.com> 1771391650 -0800\n\nrefactor(norm-rules): Standardize naming for implementation-defined behaviors\n\nConvert normative rule parameter definitions to use impl-def-behavior\nproperty and uppercase naming convention to align with Parameter SIG\nrequirements.\n\nChanges:\n- Uppercase 205 normative rule names with impl-def-behavior: true across\n  11 YAML files (counters, f-st-ext, hypervisor, machine, priv-csrs,\n  smctr, supervisor, v-st-ext, zc, zihintntl, zilsd)\n- Convert hyphens to underscores in all uppercased names\n- Replace \"kind: parameter\" with \"impl-def-behavior: true\" (61 entries\n  in machine.yaml)\n- Update 11 normative tag names to use underscores instead of hyphens\n  in both YAML definitions and AsciiDoc source files for consistency\n- Remove \"instances\" field from pmp_granularity_param rule\n- Update terminology from \"parameters\" to \"implementation-defined\n  behaviors\" in tagging_normative_rules.adoc\n\nFiles affected:\n- 11 YAML normative rule definition files\n- 5 AsciiDoc source files (hypervisor, machine, supervisor, v-st-ext,\n  zihintntl)\n- Updated reference JSON files for norm tags\n- Added documentation files: normative_rule_name_changes.md,\n  tag_name_changes.md\n\nAll changes validated with `make build-norm-rules` - builds successfully\nwith pattern ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+$ enforced for impl-def-behavior names.\n\nExamples:\n- misa_csr_implemented → MISA_CSR_IMPLEMENTED\n- satp-asidlen → SATP_ASIDLEN\n- critical-error → CRITICAL_ERROR\n- kind: parameter → impl-def-behavior: true\n- norm:hgatp-vmid_param → norm:hgatp_vmid_param\n\nRelated to issue #2669\n\nSigned-off-by: James Ball <jameball@qti.qualcomm.com>\n",
        "verified_at": "2026-02-18T05:14:25Z"
      }
